theory.intro:
For an angle of inclination $\theta$, the trigonometric ratios are defined by a point $P(x,y)$ on a circle of radius $r=\sqrt{x^2+y^2}$ centred at the origin: $\cos\theta=\dfrac{x}{r}$, $\sin\theta=\dfrac{y}{r}$, and $\tan\theta=\dfrac{y}{x}$ when $x\ne0$. Tangent is undefined when $x=0$.

